<title>ITALY: Fiat unit has 70 pct of Brazil Cofap.</title>
<headline>Fiat unit has 70 pct of Brazil Cofap.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Fiat group's Magneti Marelli unit said it has taken a 70 percent stake in Brazilian car parts maker Cofap.</p>
<p>The statement gave no financial details of the acquisition.</p>
<p>Earlier this month Cofap declined to comment on a Brazilian newspaper report saying it was likely to sell a 40 percent voting stake to Fiat.</p>
<p>O Estado de Sao Paolo newspaper said Cofap's shareholders Nelson and Leo Kasinski were holding talks with Magneti Marelli to sell the stake in the firm for $80 million.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
